.TH CLRU_DECLARE 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_declare \- declare an uninitialised LRU cache variable with type tracking
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

clru_declare(name, KeyT, ValT);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Declares the clru_cache handle variable name. It also declares two hidden
companion type variables. Those two variables carry the KeyT and the ValT
type information into the later clru_init(), clru_get() and clru_set()
macro calls.

Call clru_init() on the variable before you use the cache.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name  Variable name for the cache handle
KeyT  Key type (for example int, char *, struct MyKey)
ValT  Value type (for example double, struct MyVal)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clru_declare(cache, int, double);
clru_init(cache, 128, NULL, NULL, NULL);
/* ... use cache ... */
clru_destroy(cache);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_declare_scoped (3),
.BR clru_init (3),
.BR clru_construct (3)
